## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design cross-region consistency with SLA targets and fault tolerance for multi-tenant streams.

## Key Concepts
- Total order per tenant across regions
- Vector clocks and regional sequence numbers
- Barrier commits, idempotent processing, and tombstones
- Fault injection and late-arrival handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Vector clock merge for per-tenant streams
function mergeVC(a, b) {
  const keys = new Set([...Object.keys(a), ...Object.keys(b)]);
  const out = {};
  for (const k of keys) {
    out[k] = Math.max(a[k] || 0, b[k] || 0);
  }
  return out;
}

// Regional sequencer generates monotonically increasing sequence
class RegionalSequencer {
  constructor(region) {
    this.region = region;
    this.sequences = new Map(); // tenantId -> sequence number
  }

  next(tenantId) {
    const current = this.sequences.get(tenantId) || 0;
    const next = current + 1;
    this.sequences.set(tenantId, next);
    return { tenantId, sequence: next, region: this.region };
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests dynamic runtime schemas, non-blocking fetch, and routing on validation failure in KCNA pipelines.

## Key Concepts

- KCNA message with schemaId and payload
- Runtime schema fetch and TTL cache
- Per-message versioned validation and routing
- Safe error handling without blocking processing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: basic runtime validator setup using a cache and Ajv
class SchemaCache {
  constructor(fetcher, ttlMs = 60000) {
    this.fetcher = fetcher; this.ttl = ttlMs; this.store = new Map();
  }
  async get(version) {
    const entry = this.store.get(version);
    const now = Date.now();
    if (entry && (now - entry.ts) < this.ttl) return entry.validate;
    const schema = await this.fetcher(version);
    const Ajv = require('ajv');
    const ajv = new Ajv();
    const validate = ajv.compile(schema);
    this.store.set(version, { ts: now, validate });
    return validate;
  }
}

// usage sketch
const cache = new SchemaCache(async (v) => fetch(`/schemas/events/${v}.json`).then(r => r.json()));
async function onMessage(msg) {
  const { schemaId, payload } = msg.value;
  const validate = await cache.get(schemaId);
  const ok = validate(payload);
  if (ok) publish('validated_events', payload); else publish('invalid_events', payload);
}
```

